{"name":"Crucible","hex":"#555b59","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crucible","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cup-shaped piece of laboratory equipment used to contain chemical compounds when heating them to very high temperatures.","A heat-resistant container in which metals are melted, usually at temperatures above 500°C, commonly made of graphite with clay as a binder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crucible"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crucible","blocks":[{"text":"A crucible is a container in which metals or other substances are melted or subjected to very high temperatures. Although crucibles have historically tended to be made out of clay, they can be made from any material that withstands temperatures high enough to melt or otherwise alter its contents."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Czochralski_method_used_crucible_1.jpg/330px-Czochralski_method_used_crucible_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crucible"},{"title":"Crucible (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Crucible was a free-to-play multiplayer third-person shooter developed and published by Relentless Studios, a subsidiary of Amazon Game Studios. It is Amazon's first major original title published by their gaming division, which had previously focused on tablet games, and began development in 2014. It became available for purchase on May 20, 2020, for Windows. The game returned to a closed beta status on June 30, 2020. On October 9, 2020, Relentless Studios announced that development would be discontinued. The game's servers shut down in November 2020."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/10/Crucible_%28video_game%29_logo.svg/330px-Crucible_%28video_game%29_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crucible_(video_game)"}],"images":[{"srcset":